  "subtype": "success",
  "answer": "ANSWER: North American Aviation. In 1965 it revised the oxygen tank heater specification to 65 volts. Oxygen tank No. 2's thermostatic switches were built to a 1962 specification for 28 volts DC and were never changed, so they failed under 65-volt power. North American's documentation reviews also missed that the switches had not been updated. The tank itself was built by its subcontractor, Beech Aircraft.\nFILES: index.md, topics/oxygen-tank-2.md, areas/north-american-aviation.md",
